.TH OLLAMUX 1 "2026-08-30" "ollamux 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ollamux \- key-rotating reverse proxy for the Ollama Cloud API
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ollamux
.RB [ \-\-addr
.IR HOST:PORT ]
.RB [ \-\-keys
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.br
.B ollamux
.B \-\-help
.br
.B ollamux
.B \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ollamux
gives several Ollama Cloud API keys and serves them combined behind one
local endpoint. Requests are spread across keys (round-robin,
least-loaded first), and when a key is rate-limited, rejected, or
invalid, the request silently retries on the next key before anything
reaches the client.
.PP
This is not a local Ollama server: it serves no models, it proxies to
.I https://ollama.com\fR.
Point Ollama clients at it via
.B OLLAMA_HOST=http://localhost:11435\fR,
or OpenAI-compatible clients via base URL
.IR http://localhost:11435/v1 .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-addr " " \fIHOST:PORT\fR
Listen address. Default:
.IR 127.0.0.1:11435 .
The default port deliberately differs from Ollama's 11434 so both can
run side by side.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-keys " " \fIPATH\fR
Keys file. Default, in order of precedence: the
.B OLLAMUX_KEYS
environment variable (newline- or comma-separated keys), then
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/ollamux/keys\fR,
then
.IR ~/.config/ollamux/keys .
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Verbose stderr logging: upstream error snippets and cooldown
transitions. Without it, one summary line per request is emitted.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.SH KEYS FILE
One API key per line (get keys at
.IR https://ollama.com/settings/keys ).
Blank lines and lines starting with
.B #
are ignored. Optionally append
.B :N
to a key to set that account's per-key concurrency limit \- the number
of cloud models the account may run at once (free tier 1, pro 3, max
10; the default when no suffix is given is 3):
.PP
.RS
.nf
your-free-key...:1
your-pro-key...:3
your-max-key...:10
.fi
.RE
.PP
Requests beyond a key's concurrency limit queue briefly rather than
hammering upstream; waiters beyond that get an honest 429. Duplicate
key entries and invalid concurrency counts are startup errors, not
warnings. The file should be readable only by the user running ollamux:
.B chmod 600 ~/.config/ollamux/keys\fR.
.SH ENDPOINTS
.TS
tab(|);
l l.
/api/*|Proxied to https://ollama.com with key rotation
/v1/*|Proxied (OpenAI-compatible surface) with rotation
/_keys|Per-key health JSON (key suffixes only, no secrets)
/_health|Liveness JSON: {"ok":...,"keys":...,"total_slots":...}
.TE
.PP
Any other path answers 404 with a hint.
.SH FAILOVER BEHAVIOR
Rate-limited keys (429) cool down for 60 seconds, or the server's
.B Retry-After
value capped at 5 minutes; the request retries on the next key.
Invalid keys (401/403) are marked dead until restart. Upstream 5xx and
network errors fail over to the next key; three consecutive failures
put a key in cooldown. Everything else (e.g. a 400 from a malformed
request) is passed through untouched. Failover happens before the first
response byte, so streaming responses (NDJSON and SSE) are never
corrupted mid-flight.
.PP
Response headers identify the serving key
.B X-Ollamux-Key
(suffix only) and the retry count
.BR X-Ollamux-Retries .
.SH SIGNALS
.B SIGINT
(ctrl-c) or
.B SIGTERM
starts a graceful drain of in-flight requests for up to 5 seconds
before exit; a second signal force-quits immediately (exit code 130).
.SH SECURITY
The proxy has no authentication: anything that can reach the listen
address can use your API quota. The default binds the loopback
interface only; do not expose it further. Keep the keys file
owner-readable (0600); ollamux warns at startup if it is group- or
world-readable.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/ollamux/keys
Default keys file (honours
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ).
.TP
.I /etc/ollamux/keys
Conventional location for system-wide deployments (see
.BR systemd.unit (5)
and the shipped
.IR ollamux.service ).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OLLAMUX_KEYS
API keys, newline- or comma-separated; overrides the keys file unless
.B \-\-keys
is given.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for the default keys location.
.TP
.B OLLAMA_HOST
Not read by ollamux; exported by clients to point them at the proxy
(example:
.BR http://localhost:11435 ).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Clean shutdown after drain.
.TP
.B 2
Command-line usage error.
.TP
.B 1
Startup failure: unparseable or missing keys, unbindable address.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted: second SIGINT during drain.
.SH SEE ALSO
The project README at
.IR https://github.com/j-stechmann/ollamux .
.SH BUGS
Report issues at
